Design a test for the following execution path.

FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: quickSort
Signature: void quickSort(int arr[], int low, int high)
Description: /**
 * @brief Sorts an array of integers in ascending order using quicksort.
 *
 * Recursively sorts the subarrays defined by the indices low and high,
 * partitioning the array around a pivot at each step. The sorting is performed
 * in-place and modifies the contents of the input array.
 *
 * @param arr Array of integers to sort. Must not be NULL.
 * @param low Starting index of the subarray to sort (inclusive).
 * @param high Ending index of the subarray to sort (inclusive). Must be >= low.
 *
 * @return None.
 *
 * @note The contents of arr are modified in-place.
 *
 * @see partition
 */
Dependencies: partition, quickSort

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called quickSort
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

// Forward declarations for dependency functions
int partition (int arr[], int low, int high);
void swap(int* a, int* b);

// Target function implementation
void quickSort(int arr[], int low, int high)
{
    if (low < high) {
        int i = partition(arr, low, high);
        quickSort(arr, low, i - 1);
        quickSort(arr, i + 1, high);
    }
}

```

TARGET EXECUTION PATH:
Path 1: START | START --> CONDITION | if-else head --> STATEMENT | (low < high) --> STATEMENT | int i = partition(arr, low, high); --> STATEMENT | quickSort(arr, low, i - 1); --> STATEMENT | quickSort(arr, i + 1, high); --> MERGE | if-else merge --> RETURN | implicit return

IMPORTANT: Choose inputs that satisfy this path's conditions.

